1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,314
McDonald's million-dollar Monopoly winners

2
00:00:02,324 --> 00:00:04,447
were picked in an airport bathroom stall.

3
00:00:04,572 --> 00:00:06,394
By the man hired to protect them.

4
00:00:06,545 --> 00:00:07,487
Jerry Jacobson.

5
00:00:07,497 --> 00:00:08,033
Ex-cop.

6
00:00:08,043 --> 00:00:09,705
Head of security for the company running

7
00:00:09,715 --> 00:00:10,457
the game.

8
00:00:10,557 --> 00:00:11,162
His job?

9
00:00:11,172 --> 00:00:13,055
Escort the winning pieces, with an auditor

10
00:00:13,065 --> 00:00:14,422
watching his every move.

11
00:00:14,594 --> 00:00:16,175
Then a supplier slipped up, and mailed

12
00:00:16,185 --> 00:00:18,273
Jerry a box of tamper-proof seals.

13
00:00:18,348 --> 00:00:20,323
Now he could reseal the envelopes, and

14
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:21,517
nobody would know.

15
00:00:21,629 --> 00:00:23,546
So he'd slip into airport stalls...

16
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:25,169
and swap the winners for duds.

17
00:00:25,226 --> 00:00:26,133
Then he sold them.

18
00:00:26,143 --> 00:00:26,772
To family.

19
00:00:26,782 --> 00:00:27,364
To friends.

20
00:00:27,374 --> 00:00:28,952
To strangers paying cash.

21
00:00:29,106 --> 00:00:30,930
For years, almost every top prize went

22
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:31,662
to his network.

23
00:00:31,672 --> 00:00:33,343
Over twenty million dollars.

24
00:00:33,508 --> 00:00:35,646
Then an anonymous tip reached the FBI.

25
00:00:35,656 --> 00:00:37,513
Jerry got thirty-seven months.

26
00:00:37,775 --> 00:00:39,843
Prosecutors say even the million-dollar

27
00:00:39,853 --> 00:00:41,457
piece mailed to a children's hospital

28
00:00:41,467 --> 00:00:42,569
came from Jerry.

29
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:44,155
So next time you peel one...

30
00:00:44,165 --> 00:00:45,617
ask who touched it first.

